# browser-profile IS included in the build context (baked into the image —
# see Dockerfile) since that's the actual logged-in session now. Only the
# regenerable, session-irrelevant caches inside it are excluded, to keep
# the image smaller — Chromium rebuilds these on first use with zero effect
# on auth. The Singleton* files are OS-level lock artifacts from whatever
# local process last had the profile open; stale ones can make Chromium
# think it's already running.
browser-profile/Default/Cache
browser-profile/Default/Code Cache
browser-profile/Default/GPUCache
browser-profile/GraphiteDawnCache
browser-profile/BrowserMetrics-spare.pma
browser-profile/SingletonLock
browser-profile/SingletonSocket
browser-profile/SingletonCookie
browser-profile/RunningChromeVersion
